# Pairs with AckedWriteDurable. An abandoned append is acknowledged rather than
# faulted, so a call that then settles without landing leaves an acknowledged
# write nothing durable holds. The base faults the acknowledgement of every
# abandoned append (an unknown outcome to its caller).
MODULE: AckedWriteDurableAbandonAcknowledges
TARGET: AckedWriteDurable
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: an abandoned append is acknowledged, then settles as a hole
PERTURBS: Abandon

--- FIND
    /\ orphans' = orphans \cup {o}
    /\ UNCHANGED hidden
    /\ resyncing' = IF resyncing = "no" THEN "resync" ELSE resyncing
    /\ faults' = faults + 1
    /\ UNCHANGED <<next, occ, tail, acked>>
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the abandoned append is acknowledged.
    /\ orphans' = orphans \cup {o}
    /\ UNCHANGED hidden
    /\ resyncing' = IF resyncing = "no" THEN "resync" ELSE resyncing
    /\ faults' = faults + 1
    /\ acked' = acked \cup {o}
    /\ UNCHANGED <<next, occ, tail>>
--- END
